workspace/012-tyreseluo0630-75216a25af14/scaffold/README.md:13:| `lib/arc.js` §Store | records shared through the server, sign-in and view state per browser | every browser session reads the same records (another user's isolated session, a later visit, the same URL reopened), so what one session creates the next one sees; `ARC.state.session` (the signed-in user) stays in its own browser session, `ARC.state.ui` and other non-record keys in its tab; every key declared in `seed.js` and every array is a shared record collection; reads and writes are synchronous, so screens still render in the click's task |
workspace/012-tyreseluo0630-75216a25af14/scaffold/README.md:17:| `lib/arc.js` §Popover | `openPopover(host, items, {kind, id, label})` / `closePopover()` | renders inside the supplied host (apps find the record or cell a command acts on through the menu's ancestors); the requirements decide its scope and whether a command opens a named entity editor; native buttons by default, explicit menu/menuitem roles only for a required menu. A menu closes after one of its items runs unless the action opened another popover: a menu left open inside a grid cell becomes part of the cell's text (`PenCopyCutPaste` after a menu Cut) |
workspace/012-tyreseluo0630-75216a25af14/scaffold/README.md:19:| `lib/arc.js` §Presses | `ARC.render()` waits during a left-button press | the browser sends `click` (and `dblclick` on the second press) only to an element still in the document at release; a render in a mousedown/mouseup handler replaces it, so a re-rendered grid cell never receives a click and no double-click editor opens. The render runs at the end of the click sequence, same task; an editor a dblclick handler wrote itself is kept |
workspace/012-tyreseluo0630-75216a25af14/scaffold/README.md:20:| `lib/arc.js` §Clipboard | `onCopy(fn)`, `onPaste(fn)`, `copyToClipboard(cut)`, `pasteFromClipboard()` | copy/cut/paste go through the browser clipboard (tests put the text there themselves): native copy/cut/paste events outside text fields, the async clipboard API when a page listener cancelled the event and for menu commands; the text to copy is read when the keys are pressed; `data` returns with a paste of the app's own copy; a menu Paste whose clipboard read is missing, refused (no permission, as in the evaluator's browser) or silent for 400 ms pastes the app's own last copy; pasted text arrives with `\n` line ends and without the final line break of copied rows |
